{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>A land flowing with milk and honey.</b> The verse is abbreviated, and this is what it says: <b>as HaShem your God of your fathers spoke</b> — to give <b>you a land flowing</b> etc. Another interpretation: it is deficient a bet, like what is found 'בית ה׳', and many more, and this is what it says: when you multiply greatly in a land flowing with milk and honey."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "The second interpretation reads 'ארץ זבת' as a defective form of 'ארץ זבת בחלב ודבש', citing the analogy of 'בית ה׳' for a proclitic bet that can drop; the referent of 'ועוד הרבה' is other instances of this phenomenon."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:54.208494951Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}